{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01282",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.33,
      "end_seconds": 8.17,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.31,
      "end_seconds": 13.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.62,
      "end_seconds": 20.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Good morning, uh, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.93,
      "end_seconds": 25.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.42,
      "end_seconds": 29.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "It's no real problems, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.6,
      "end_seconds": 35.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "So, can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.63,
      "end_seconds": 45.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Simvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 46.57,
      "end_seconds": 53.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "It's meant to be at night, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.35,
      "end_seconds": 65.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.89,
      "end_seconds": 69.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.17,
      "end_seconds": 74.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "About a week, give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 75.91,
      "end_seconds": 79.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer two weeks, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.15,
      "end_seconds": 84.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.92,
      "end_seconds": 87.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.44,
      "end_seconds": 91.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.57,
      "end_seconds": 111.18,
      "duration_seconds": 17.61,
      "text": "Maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day. As for bit of back stiffness, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.22,
      "end_seconds": 116.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Has there been an occasional headache too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.99,
      "end_seconds": 123.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, ten days. As for occasional headache, mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.13,
      "end_seconds": 127.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Did you notice any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.78,
      "end_seconds": 130.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "No. No weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.45,
      "end_seconds": 135.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Have you noticed chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.18,
      "end_seconds": 140.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.37,
      "end_seconds": 143.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.63,
      "end_seconds": 147.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.51,
      "end_seconds": 151.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Alright, what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.88,
      "end_seconds": 164.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol, yes. An irregular heartbeat, for nearly five years. I took the morning off to come in today. I have eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.53,
      "end_seconds": 167.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.14,
      "end_seconds": 183.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.87,
      "end_seconds": 206.31,
      "duration_seconds": 20.44,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I've never smoked in my life. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. No, I share a house with my brother. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.92,
      "end_seconds": 209.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.82,
      "end_seconds": 214.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.37,
      "end_seconds": 221.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.56,
      "end_seconds": 227.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.12,
      "end_seconds": 232.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.59,
      "end_seconds": 245.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.74,
      "end_seconds": 265.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 65, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, BP is 109 over 80, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.03,
      "end_seconds": 269.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.7,
      "end_seconds": 273.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.98,
      "end_seconds": 287.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Your heart and lungs sound normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.14,
      "end_seconds": 293.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.31,
      "end_seconds": 311.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I think we're dealing with a healthy adult with no worrying findings at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 313.61,
      "end_seconds": 315.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.75,
      "end_seconds": 337.66,
      "duration_seconds": 18.91,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a healthy adult with no worrying findings do well once it's treated properly. Just to be sure I understood. You've had no real problems, and no weight loss or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.5,
      "end_seconds": 340.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.18,
      "end_seconds": 378.39,
      "duration_seconds": 28.21,
      "text": "Let's book a fasting sugar test to look into routine check. We should do a cholesterol blood test for routine check. Keep up regular exercise and a balanced diet. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. The thing that would worry me is if new symptoms appear. If that happens, go to emergency. I'll want another look in twelve months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.9,
      "end_seconds": 383.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.42,
      "end_seconds": 386.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.62,
      "end_seconds": 390.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.06,
      "end_seconds": 395.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}